[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High-level requirements of the analyser item, part ANL: the analyser framework (base class, registry, flight
phases, vehicle identification, shared helpers), the GPS, battery, motor, board power and parameter checks, the
shipped parameter tables and the script that generates them. Written from the code as built. The oscillation,
vibration, EKF and ascent checks are in another part. Low-level requirements are in `llr-anl.sdoc`; the design
is in `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-anl.md`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Framework

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One interface for every check
STATEMENT: >>>
Every check shall be a class with a unique snake_case name, a display name, a declaration of the topics, columns
and log formats it needs and a score weight, and one operation that takes the topic tables and the parameter set
and returns one result holding its findings, a health score from 0 to 100, its headline numbers, and whether it
was skipped and why.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-018

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Missing declared inputs give a skipped result with the reason
STATEMENT: >>>
When a required topic is absent, none of a set of alternative topics is present, the log format is not one the
check declares, or a present topic lacks a declared column, the check shall not run and shall return a skipped
result whose reason names what is missing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A failing check does not stop the others
STATEMENT: >>>
An exception raised inside a check shall be turned into a skipped result whose reason carries the exception type
and message, and every result shall carry the time the check took in milliseconds.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test in the analyser test files makes `analyse` raise. Review checks the `try`/`except Exception` in
`BaseAnalyser.safe_analyse` and that `processing_ms` is set on both paths.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The set of checks: nine built-ins plus plugins
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall supply fresh instances of the nine built-in checks in a fixed order (oscillation, vibration, EKF,
battery, GPS, parameters, motors, ascent profile, board power), followed by every plugin class found under the
entry point group `flightmd.analysers`, each given the flight metadata of the log.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-018

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bad plugins are left out with a warning
STATEMENT: >>>
A plugin that fails to load, is not a subclass of the check base class, reuses the name of a built-in or of an
earlier plugin, or fails to construct shall be left out and a warning naming it shall be logged; the remaining
checks shall still be supplied.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-018

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Score weights
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall publish the score weight of each check by name, leaving out checks of weight 0. The built-in
weights shall be oscillation 20, vibration 20, EKF 20, battery 15, GPS 15, parameters 5, motors 5 (sum 100) and
ascent profile 0 and board power 0. A plugin's weight shall be added to the set unchanged, so the total then
exceeds 100.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-018

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Armed and in-air windows
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall derive the armed windows from `vehicle_status.arming_state` (2 means armed) and the in-air windows
from the armed windows intersected with the not-landed windows of `vehicle_land_detected.landed`, on the
log-relative microsecond clock. With no arming data, or a log that was never armed, both shall be the whole log
and the result shall say that the phases are not known. With arming data and no usable land detector the in-air
windows shall equal the armed windows.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Autopilot and frame type from the parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall identify the autopilot (px4, ardupilot, unknown) and the frame type (multirotor, fixed_wing,
vtol, rover, unknown) from the parameter names and values, and shall give the rate-loop P and D parameter names
for an axis only for PX4 and ArduPilot multirotors and fixed-wing aircraft, giving none for VTOL, rover and
unknown vehicles.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Confidence and time window of a finding
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall provide one rule for the confidence of a finding, a number from 0 to 1 rounded to 3 places that
rises with the margin past the threshold, with the duration up to 2 s, and with the data quality, and one rule
that turns a window in microseconds into the finding's start and end in milliseconds and seconds.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests check the window start of findings (`t_start_s`). No test asserts a confidence value; review checks the
formula in `helpers.confidence` against LLR-ANL-016.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Chart series on findings
STATEMENT: >>>
Findings of the GPS, battery, motor and board power checks shall carry the time series behind them, reduced to
at most 500 points per series by taking every n-th sample, with timestamps in milliseconds and with NaN and
infinite values replaced by null.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks the checks for chart series. The web application draws them (SYS-036) and the report
must hold only valid JSON numbers (SYS-019), so the checks bound and clean the series at the source.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-019

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Module health score and fixed rules
STATEMENT: >>>
Each of the GPS, battery, motor, board power and parameter checks shall start its health score at 100 and
subtract a fixed penalty per finding (30 for a critical finding, 15 for a warning, 10 for the battery C-rate
warning), never going below 0, and shall decide every finding, severity and suggested value from constants and
tables held in the code and the shipped data files, with no random or learned element.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests check that findings lower the score and that severities follow the thresholds. Absence of random or
learned elements is checked by review of the imports and code of the five modules.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Headline numbers per check
STATEMENT: >>>
Each check shall return its headline numbers by fixed names: GPS `min_satellites` and `max_hdop`; battery
`consumed_mah`, `sag_per_cell_v`, `internal_resistance_mohm_per_cell` and `peak_c_rate`; motors
`motor_balance_index` and `motor_<n>_rpm_dev_pct`; board power `min_vcc_v` and `vcc_range_v`; parameters
`param_count` and `anomaly_count`. A number that could not be measured shall be left out, not set to zero.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: GPS check

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPS check inputs and in-flight gating
STATEMENT: >>>
The GPS check shall need the topic `vehicle_gps_position` with a `timestamp` column, shall judge only samples
inside the in-air windows, and when the phases are not known shall instead drop the samples before the first 3D
fix. It shall return a skipped result when the topic has no timestamps or fewer than 5 samples remain.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPS findings
STATEMENT: >>>
The GPS check shall report: no 3D fix at any time in flight (critical); a fix below 3D for 1.0 s or longer
(critical) or shorter (warning); a loss of 4 or more satellites within 5 s (warning); HDOP held for 2 s above
2.0 (warning) or above 4.0 (critical); a jamming indicator held for 2 s above 100 of 255 (warning) or above 180
(critical), or a receiver jamming state of warning or critical held for 2 s; and a receiver spoofing state of
"indicated" (warning) or "multiple indications" (critical) on any sample. Each finding shall carry a rule
identifier beginning `gps.`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Battery check

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Battery check inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
The battery check shall need the topic `battery_status` with a timestamp, a voltage and a current column, shall
use only rows where all three are present and the voltage is above 0, over the whole log with no flight-phase
gating, and shall return a skipped result when a column is missing or fewer than 10 such rows exist. It shall
take the cell count and the rated capacity from the log, else from the parameters, and shall estimate the cell
count from the highest voltage at 4.2 V per cell when neither gives it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Battery findings
STATEMENT: >>>
The battery check shall report: voltage sag per cell at peak load, computed from the internal resistance fitted
in 10 s windows, above 0.50 V (warning) or above 1.00 V (critical); a 1 s sustained current above 30 times the
rated capacity (warning); a capacity implied by the fall in state of charge that is more than 15 percent below
the rated capacity, when at least 30 percent of charge was used and the state of charge is not itself computed
from the drawn current (warning); and a battery temperature above 60 degrees C (warning). Each finding shall
carry a rule identifier beginning `battery.`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Motor check

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Motor check inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
The motor check shall need the topic `esc_status` with a `timestamp` column and at least one per-ESC RPM column
that reports a non-zero value, shall ignore ESC slots at or beyond `esc_count` and slots that never report
anything but zero, shall treat a missing sample as no data and never as a stopped motor, and shall return a
skipped result when there are no timestamps or no RPM telemetry. Balance and dropout rules shall apply to in-air
samples; when the phases are not known, in-air shall mean more than half of the motors above 500 RPM.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Motor findings
STATEMENT: >>>
The motor check shall report: a spread of per-motor hover RPM (standard deviation over mean) above 0.08
(warning) or above 0.15 (critical), naming the motor furthest from the mean; one motor's hover current more than
20 percent above the mean (warning); an ESC temperature above 80 degrees C (warning, one per ESC); and a motor
below 100 RPM for more than 100 ms in flight while the median of the others stays above 1000 RPM (critical, one
per motor). Each finding shall carry a rule identifier beginning `motors.`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Board power check

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Board power check
STATEMENT: >>>
The board power check shall need the topic `system_power` with a `timestamp` column and shall judge samples
inside the armed windows only. It shall report a 5 V rail reading outside 4.3 V to 5.8 V on samples not powered
from USB (critical, `power.vcc_out_of_range`) and a peripheral over-current flag (warning, `power.overcurrent`).
It shall return a skipped result when fewer than 2 samples are armed or when the topic carries no voltage and no
fault field. Its weight shall be 0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Parameter check

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameter table chosen from the firmware in the log
STATEMENT: >>>
The parameter check shall take the firmware major and minor version from the flight metadata and use the
shipped table of that autopilot (and, for ArduPilot, of that vehicle) whose version is nearest, preferring the
later one on a tie. With no version, or an ArduPilot log whose vehicle is not copter, plane or rover, it shall
use all tables of that autopilot merged to the widest range. A parameter set with no PX4 or ArduPilot marker
shall be checked against the PX4 tables. It shall return a skipped result only when the log has no parameters.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers, data
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-014
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameter range findings
STATEMENT: >>>
For every finite numeric parameter that is not read-only in the table, the parameter check shall report a value
below the firmware minimum or above the firmware maximum, and otherwise a value outside the tighter recommended
range it holds, as `params.below_range` or `params.above_range`, naming which limit was broken, the table used
when the limit is the firmware's, and the reason when the limit is a recommended one. The finding shall be
critical when the value is further outside than half the width of the usable range or is negative where the
minimum is 0 or more, else a warning. Multicopter parameters (`MC_`, `MPC_`) shall not be checked on a PX4
fixed-wing or rover.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers, data
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-014
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Risky parameter combinations
STATEMENT: >>>
The parameter check shall report the fixed list of risky combinations for the log's autopilot: on PX4 a rate P
gain above 0.3 with a rate D gain below 0.001 (roll, pitch), `MPC_XY_P` above 1.5 with `MPC_XY_VEL_P_ACC` below
1.5, `BAT_LOW_THR` below `BAT_CRIT_THR`, and `COM_RC_LOSS_T` below 0.5 s; on ArduPilot a low battery failsafe
not above the critical one (voltage, capacity; both set) and `ARMING_CHECK` equal to 0. A combination shall be
reported only when every parameter it names is in the log.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Suggested parameter values
STATEMENT: >>>
A range finding shall carry one suggested change for its parameter: the firmware default from the table when
that lies inside both the firmware and the recommended range, else the nearest edge of the range. A combination
finding on PX4 shall suggest the firmware default of one named parameter when a default is known and it moves
the value in the stated direction, and shall carry no suggestion otherwise. Values shall be shown and compared
in their float32 decimal form.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-024
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Suggested values held inside the range of the log's own firmware
STATEMENT: >>>
The parameter check shall hold every suggested value inside the metadata range of the parameter for the firmware
version in the log, and shall withhold the suggestion with a note when no table of that version is shipped or
the value cannot be held inside the range.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
As built, the suggestion for `BAT_LOW_THR` in the inverted-threshold combination is not bounded by the
maximum, and suggestions are bounded by the nearest or merged table, which may not be the firmware in the log.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-016

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Parameter tables

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Shipped parameter tables
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall ship one JSON table per firmware series: PX4 1.13, 1.14 and 1.15, and ArduPilot Copter, Plane and
Rover 4.6 and 4.7. Each table shall record the autopilot, the vehicle, the exact firmware version, the address
the metadata came from and the date generated, and shall map each parameter name to whichever of default,
minimum, maximum, unit, type, reboot-required and read-only the metadata gives. The item shall also ship the
hand-kept recommended ranges, each with its reason.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests load every table and use the fields. The list of files and their headers is checked by review of
`flightmd_core/data/param_tables/`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: data, analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-039
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ANL-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Tables generated from the firmware projects' metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
A script shall build the parameter tables from the metadata the firmware projects publish: the PX4
`parameters.xml` of each listed release and the ArduPilot `apm.pdef.xml` of the latest stable release of the two
newest series of each vehicle. It shall write each table in full or not at all, one parameter per line, and
shall exit with status 1 and name what failed when a source could not be fetched or parsed.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test runs the script (it needs the network). Review checks `scripts/gen_param_tables.py` against LLR-ANL-088
to LLR-ANL-094 and that the shipped tables carry the headers it writes.
<<<
ALLOCATION: tools, data
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-039

